.TH PAWS 1 "September 2026" "paws 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paws \- menu-driven SLSsteam manager for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paws
[\fB\-w\fP] [\fIcommand\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paws
opens the full-screen TUI in the terminal you run it in. Give it a subcommand for the
command-line interface instead. With
.B \-\-window
(or when started with no terminal at all, like from an app menu) it opens a new terminal
window running paws.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-window
Open paws in a new terminal window instead of the current one. The terminal is picked from
$PAWS_TERMINAL, the one you are typing in, $TERMINAL, then whatever of kitty, konsole,
alacritty, foot, wezterm, ... is installed. If one fails to start, the next is tried and its
error is printed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B menu
Open the full-screen TUI in this terminal (default when run interactively).
.TP
.B launch
Show how paws opens and which terminal \fB\-\-window\fP would use.
.TP
.B doctor
Preflight checks. \fBpaws doctor \-\-fix\fP adds config keys SLSsteam expects.
.TP
.B settings
Show or change settings: \fBpaws settings nsfw on|off\fP,
\fBpaws settings random on|off\fP,
\fBpaws settings launch <cmd>\fP,
\fBpaws settings features\fP.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PAWS_TERMINAL
Force the terminal emulator used by \fB\-\-window\fP.
